A||||6||Seanh||Valve Lash Adjustment||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||11-04-2000||01:47 PM||||Im not the brightest marker in the box, so I have a few questions. I am ready to put the heads back in the car, and I am having trouble with the Haynes manuals explination of valve lash adjustments. I am supposed to turn the engine to the no. 1 firing position right? Then twirl the approite rod and tighten the rocker arm bolt until no play is felt, right? Thats what Im getting from it, but I thought I would check.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">   <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>If you smoke after sex, your doing it way to fast.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Greg Piet||11-04-2000||02:45 PM||||You pretty much got it!<BR>I have an old thread in here where everyone explains it to me.<P>I actually spun the rods untill i couldnt rotate them anymore by hand but that resulted in overtightening at times, so I guess I was too aggressive at turning the pushrod.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||11-04-2000||03:32 PM||||turn the crank until one valve is in the up position, tighten the rocker arm until there is snugness of the rod, then tighten one and a half turns more (no more or less) -- do this for each valve by repeating the above procedure - in other words, tighten each one when that respective valve is up..........that should do it.......<P>------------------<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                            <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>www.http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||11-04-2000||05:08 PM||||If you just have the heads on and the intake off, turn to each mark on the harmonic balancer starting with # 1 intake and so on like the book says. Take a visual look at the lifter it's self and watch the center of it. As soon as it starts to move down (watch closely!), play is removed 1 to 1 1/2 turns more. DO NOT tighten any more than that, this will center the tappet in it's travel and will produce the best top end lubrication. it is best to do this with DRY parts and no lubrication so that you can 'feel the drag' if your turning the push rod as well. The push rod will not stop turning until it gets to the bottom of travel in the lifter, this is NOT WHAT YOU WANT! Pay attention to what your doing and you should be fine!||||reg||14
Z||000004||Ironhorse||11-04-2000||06:08 PM||||*WARNING* myself and few other people that have owns fiero have this situation where the car run like crap where do 1 and half turn after 0 valve lash.  We all including myself went back into our fiero and redid it again only this time we turn it half turn after 0 lash.  Our fiero runs perfectly and smoothly. I could not get my car to run for more than 2 min when I had it set 1 1/2 after 0 lash.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||11-04-2000||11:39 PM||||Any feedback on that one? I dont want to get the car all back together and have it run like crap. Has anyone else had this problem?<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">   <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>If you smoke after sex, your doing it way to fast.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||11-05-2000||12:15 AM||||I usually try to set the valves with the intake off so I can see the push rod starting to move the plunger back down into the lifter as I tighten it. I take out the slack and then go maybe a quarter round after that. Usually the repair manual will tell which lifters can be tightened down at which intervals. On my 3.4, I cheated a little. I kept the pushrods in the right order and just tightened the rockers back down to where the shiny marks on the push rods matched back up with the guide plate. No noises and it runs very good.||||reg||1
